A2Billing 3.0 (nixonch): MySQL 8.x installation
===============================================

Run the commands from the project root. The database must be empty.

1. Set the database name, application username and password in
   DataBase/mysql-8.x/a2billing-createdb-user.sql, then run as a MySQL administrator:

   mysql -u root -p < DataBase/mysql-8.x/a2billing-createdb-user.sql

2. Run the installer:

   bash DataBase/mysql-8.x/install-db.sh

   Enter the database name, hostname, MySQL administrator username and password.

3. Copy a2billing.conf to /etc/a2billing.conf and configure its [database] section:

   [database]
   hostname = localhost
   port = 3306
   user = a2billinguser
   password = YOUR_PASSWORD
   dbname = mya2billing
   dbtype = mysql

   Use the database name, application username and password chosen in step 1.

Currency catalog
----------------

Initial currency data uses the ISO 4217 monetary list published by SIX on
2026-09-17. Funds, metals, special units and the internal VED redenomination
code are excluded; VES remains the code for current Venezuelan transactions
under SIX Amendment 170. Rates are Frankfurter reference rates dated
2026-11-09/10 in USD.
Run Cronjobs/currencies_update.php after configuring the installation to
refresh rates in the configured base currency.
Currency rates use DECIMAL(17,10) so weak currencies are not rounded to zero
or forced to an inaccurate minimum rate. The migration expands older
cc_currencies.value columns before saving the new rates.

For an existing MySQL installation, preview and apply the catalog migration:

    php DataBase/mysql-8.x/sync-currencies.php
    php DataBase/mysql-8.x/sync-currencies.php --apply

The migration fetches current rates, preserves IDs for existing currencies,
adds missing currencies, and removes obsolete currencies and metals only
after checking currency references. It stops without changing data if any
currency to remove is still used. --config=/path/to/a2billing.conf selects
another installation. Run under the same account as the currency cron job.

